<title>GERMANY: Deutsche Luxembourg to set up Irish unit.</title>
<headline>Deutsche Luxembourg to set up Irish unit.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Bank Luxembourg S.A., a unit of Germany's giant Deutsche Bank AG, on Friday said it had set up a fully-owned subsidiary in Dublin, Ireland.</p>
<p>The new bank, to start operations April 1, will have starting capital resources of 200 million marks and will be mainly involved in euro-loan business, Deutsche said in a statement released in Frankfurt.</p>
<p>The unit, Deutsche Bank, DB Ireland plc, will be based in Dublin's International Financial Services Centre.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
